  "ownership": [
    "Backend model preparation owns an allocation-free payload plan covering raw/decoded/stacked/rotary storage, host staging and ownership tables. Stacked preparation includes old/new GPU payload overlap. Explicit peak caps reject before any upload.",
    "Transformer request/coordinator plans share preparation validation and tensor allocation walks. Backend callbacks own embedding, A8 input and attention workspace byte queries. Scalar view width crosses the backend metadata boundary and remains quant-registry data.",
    "Combined group-workspace budgets conservatively charge both host and device; these are upper bounds rather than exact per-space measurements.",
    "The scheduler-owned pure ledger supports staged shared setup, read-only active feasibility and generation-renewed idle replacement with old-retained plus new-preparation overlap. The transformer does not depend on the scheduler.",
    "The CLI pool keeps capacity rounding and smallest-adequate idle reuse. It proves active feasibility before evicting idle storage. When overlap fits, dense KV grows in place; otherwise idle storage is destroyed before fresh preparation. Active leases are never evicted.",
